      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Lake City earned its name from nearby Lake Creek, a modest waterway that once fed a pond east of town.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lake_City%2C_Iowa",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Lake City only had about 250 residents until 1881, when the arrival of the Chicago and Northwestern Railroad ushered in a boom time.",
